WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
A scene of upheaval gives way to the weighing of deeds. Read this five-movement arrangement as a proposed thematic map.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.000
5 thematic movements in this study arrangement. The labels summarize passages; they are not Quran translations.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:25.000
The opening asks about the striking event. The closing image intensifies its consequences. Their connection here is an editorial study proposal.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Images of a world losing its stability precede the weighing of deeds; a renewed question follows. Compare these transitions without assuming identical language.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Verses 101:6–9 contrast heavy and light scales and their outcomes. In this arrangement they form the thematic hinge.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The connecting marks gather into nested rings. Their symmetry visualizes this reading; it does not establish the reading by itself.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:00.000
What changes when the weighing of deeds is read between the surah’s questions and images?
